 "note": "Cutting a shared value out of the NVFP4 activation quantize. The kernel RMS-normalizes its input and encodes the result, so the normalizer feeds the encode's every branch, and the cut materializes it into a workspace the rest of the kernel reads back.\n\nThe read is the point. A lowered body reads producer names throughout, so an edge's result name is what the emitted kernel declares -- and the cut replaces the occurrences of ONE cone object, while a structurally equal cone elsewhere in the same kernel keeps computing that value in place under the same name. Naming the workspace read after the cone rather than after the workspace therefore declares one name twice in one scope, from two different sources, which nvcc rejects. So this case earns its keep at `built`: the schedule realizes either way, and only the compiler accepts or refuses the source.\n\nevidence: the same route is what `tune` proposes on the Qwen3-8B-NVFP4 decode trunk, where it reached nvcc as `\"v23\" has already been declared in the current scope` and cost the candidate its measurement.",
